TEXT -256 -232 Left 3 ;#61 Capacitive sampler
TEXT -256 -176 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Kk_N_TpDeo
TEXT -256 -136 Left 2 ;Ctap couples the through line into a 50 ohm sampling port. With no resistor across the line, the tap\nloads the through path far less, and the sample rises with frequency instead of being flat.
TEXT 760 -16 Left 2 !.tran 0 20u 10u 0.5n
TEXT 760 40 Left 2 !.meas tran THROUGH_RMS RMS V(RF_THROUGH)
TEXT 760 80 Left 2 !.meas tran SAMPLE_RMS RMS V(SAMPLE_OUT)
TEXT 760 160 Left 2 ;Alan writes no value on this drawing\neither. In the coaxial fittings he shows,\nthe coupling is set by the probe's\nphysical size and spacing, so 5 pF\nstands for a small stray capacitance.
TEXT 760 352 Left 2 ;The .meas window is the whole saved\ninterval, 10 us to 20 us, which the .tran\ndirective already sets.
